Third-party component not covered by this License
-------------------------------------------------

The Samsung Health Sensor SDK (samsung-health-sensor-api-*.aar) is proprietary to Samsung Electronics
and is NOT part of this repository. Each developer downloads it from Samsung under Samsung's own license
(see wear/libs/README.md). That license, not the GPL, governs the SDK — including its restrictions on

demonstrated. This project is therefore published as source code only.

The phone app includes sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx) and the ONNX Runtime it
bundles (MIT). The optional neural voice model is not in this repository or the app: tools/voice/fetch_voice_model.sh
downloads Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0) with espeak-ng data (GPL-3.0).

To install the watch app from the phone, the phone app includes Kadb (Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/flyfishxu/Kadb), spake2-java (GPL-3.0, https://github.com/Flyfish233/spake2-java), Bouncy Castle
(MIT, https://www.bouncycastle.org) and Okio (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/square/okio). A phone app built with the
Samsung SDK also carries the watch app, and with it the SDK, so the rule above applies to it too.

The :samsung-health-stub module is original OpenTDI code that mirrors the SDK's public API (as
documented in Samsung's public API reference) so the project compiles without the SDK; it contains
no Samsung code.


